    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today centers on a favorable exposure to Cody Bradford, whose 5.29 xERA makes him the primary target for our lineup. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 82.37 score, fueled by his plus matchup against Bryce Elder and the inherent advantage of batting second. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier is **Tyler Soderstrom**, who benefits significantly from the park factors and SP weakness, sporting a 74.23 efficiency rating. We are also capitalizing on the platoon advantage against Bradford with **Max Muncy** (68.95) and **Henry Bolte** (65.40). While **Muncy** faces a slight penalty for hitting seventh, his high SP skill adjustment makes him a high-upside play, while **Bolte** gains a massive 10% boost from his projected leadoff spot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the periphery involved **Travis Bazzana**, who landed on the bench with a 42.70 score. While **Bazzana** offers viable utility, he ultimately fell short of the threshold compared to the platoon-heavy upside provided by **Isaac Paredes** (54.18), whose dynamic platoon edge against Bryan Woo made him the safer choice to round out the UTIL slot. Meanwhile, we remain wary of the risk surrounding **Brice Turang**; despite his 46.98 score, he faces a daunting matchup against Tarik Skubal. However, we are holding **Brice Turang** in the lineup due to his high-leverage speed profile, as Skubal\u2019s slower delivery provides a crucial 4% boost to his stolen base potential\u2014an essential consideration for our scarcity-driven strategy. \n\nManagers should keep a close eye on the official lineups, as all selections remain based on projected spots. We are closely monitoring **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Cole Young**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Mickey Moniak** for any last-minute defensive adjustments that could shift their batting order and dilute their expected efficiency scores. **James Wood** remains sidelined on the IL, but our bench depth\u2014including **Jose Caballero**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Edwin Arroyo**\u2014is ready to deploy if game caps permit or matchups improve tomorrow.",
